  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "string-definition",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-strings",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-1447528d9989"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-1447528d9989",
          "exact": "In computer programming, a string is traditionally a sequence of characters, either as a literal constant or as some kind of variable. The latter may allow its elements to be mutated and the length changed, or it may be fixed (after creation). A string is often implemented as an array data structure of bytes (or words) that stores a sequence of elements, typically characters, using some character encoding."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-1447528d9989",
          "subject": "string",
          "predicate": "is_defined_as",
          "object": "sequence of characters, either literal constant or variable (elements mutable, length changeable, or fixed after creation), often implemented as array data structure of bytes (or words) storing character-encoded elements"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "claim 是引文 [0,409) 的完整忠实转述：'a string is traditionally a sequence of characters, either as a literal constant or as some kind of variable' 对应『字符串传统上是字符序列，可作为字面量常量或某种变量』；'The latter may allow its elements to be mutated and the length changed, or it may be fixed (after creation)' 对应『后者允许元素被修改与长度改变，也可能在创建后固定』；'often implemented as an array data structure of bytes (or words) ... using some character encoding' 对应『常实现为字节（或字）的数组数据结构，用某种字符编码存储字符元素序列』。分句一一对应，无添加无曲解，判定 supported。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-strings",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-1447528d9989",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 409
        }
      ],
      "independence": {
        "group_id": "independence_unknown",
        "basis": []
      }
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "string-representation",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-strings",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-812fbabfc66a"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-812fbabfc66a",
          "exact": "Strings are typically implemented as arrays of bytes, characters, or code units, to allow fast access to individual units or substrings, including characters when they have a fixed length. A few languages such as Haskell implement them as linked lists instead."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-812fbabfc66a",
          "subject": "string",
          "predicate": "typically_implemented_as",
          "object": "arrays of bytes, characters, or code units (fast access to individual units or substrings); a few languages such as Haskell implement them as linked lists"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文 [0,260) 与 claim 逐句对应：'arrays of bytes, characters, or code units' 对应『字节、字符或码元（code unit）数组』；'to allow fast access to individual units or substrings' 对应『以便快速访问单个单元或子串』；'A few languages such as Haskell implement them as linked lists instead' 对应『少数语言（如 Haskell）用链表实现』。claim 未复述引文关于定长字符的补充从句，属信息裁剪而非出入，所陈述内容均被引文直接支撑，判定 supported。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-strings",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-812fbabfc66a",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 260
        }
