    {
      "claim_id": "string-editor-repr",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-strings",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0ba90d1d9d6c"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0ba90d1d9d6c",
          "exact": "The core data structure in a text editor is the one that manages the string (sequence of characters) that represents the current state of the file being edited. While that state could be stored in a single long consecutive array of characters, a typical text editor instead uses an alternative representation as its sequence data structure—a gap buffer, a linked list of lines, a piece table, or a rope—which makes certain string operations, such as insertions, deletions, and undoing previous edits, more efficient."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0ba90d1d9d6c",
          "subject": "text editor core data structure",
          "predicate": "is",
          "object": "string managing current file state, typically stored via alternative representations (gap buffer, linked list of lines, piece table, or rope) making insertions, deletions, and undoing previous edits more efficient than a single long consecutive character array"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文 [0,518) 完整覆盖 claim：'The core data structure in a text editor is the one that manages the string ... that represents the current state of the file being edited' 对应『文本编辑器的核心数据结构是管理代表当前文件状态的字符串』；'a single long consecutive array of characters' 对应『单个连续字符数组』；'a gap buffer, a linked list of lines, a piece table, or a rope' 对应『gap buffer、行链表、piece table 或 rope』；'makes certain string operations, such as insertions, deletions, and undoing previous edits, more efficient' 对应『使插入、删除与撤销等操作更高效』。全部对应，无添加无曲解，判定 supported。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
        {
